   "text": {
    "L1": "Rama Natha believed the sage could make gold with a magic potion.",
    "L2": "That belief was wrong. The sage asked for dew because Rama Natha would not have listened to plain advice.",
    "L3": "Rama Natha collected five litres of dew from banana leaves, then planted and tended the land for six years.",
    "L4": "Madhumati sold the bananas in the market. Their hard work created the wealth, not magic.",
    "L5": "Rama Natha felt worried when money was spent, and angry when nothing happened to the copper vessel.",
    "L6": "He was surprised when Madhumati opened a box of gold coins. The coins came from selling their bananas.",
    "L7": "The message is simple: hard work brings results, while shortcuts do not.",
    "L8": "Now put the important events in the order they happened."
   },
